[? if thalmann_votes_rnd_1 > thalmann_votes + 2 and not collectivist_support_marcher: The decline of [+ communist_candidate_1932 +]'s vote share is largely attributed to the futility of his campaign, with estimates suggesting that a significant portion of his former voters have either defected to [+ royalist_candidate_1932 +] or abstained from the second round. The <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivist**</span> camp is overcome with resignation, as this outcome suggests that the Commonwealth masses are still far from ready for the revolutionary assault against capitalism that he and his party’s leadership had been preparing for. ?]

[? if dufour_run and not gallax_support_dufour: It is seen that [+ royalist_candidate_1932 +] was the one to benefit from [+ traditionalist_candidate_1932 +]'s withdrawal, rather than [+ reactionary_candidate_1932 +], having garnered 60% of his former voters. Even if [+ royalist_candidate_1932 +] doesn't win, the destruction of the parties between the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Royalists**</span> and [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionists</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] will have drastic consequences for Commonwealth democracy. ?]

@hindenburg_wins
on-arrival: president = "DuFour"; dufour_angry_bruning += 15 if not marcher_campaign and marcher_support_reactionary

As expected, the incumbent DuFour wins the presidency. Let's hope he continues to keep the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalists</span> out of power.

[? if marcher_support_reactionary and not bruning_time: The fact that, even with the votes from the <span style="color: #c00000;">Reformists</span> and <span style="color: #000000;">Faithful</span>, DuFour has failed to secure a majority in the first round has been a great embarrassment to him. Realizing that many of his former supporters have turned to Gallax, he is now shifting further to the right. ?]

[? if marcher_support_reactionary and bruning_time: The fact that [+ reactionary_candidate_1932 +] owed his reelection to the parties who opposed him in 4290 rather than those with whom he felt the closest natural affinity with is a source of great personal anguish to the aging president and severely strained his relations with Askew and the conservatives who had orchestrated his reelection campaign. ?]

@thalmann_wins
on-arrival: president = "Halsmark"; collectivist_relation = 80;

Ernst Halsmark of the <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span> has won the presidency. Immediately, the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">far</span>-<span style="color: #3E88B3;">right</span> launches a coup attempt against the government. We have no choice but to unite with the <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span> against the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Sovereigntists</span>...

- @civil_war: This is civil war.

@hitler_wins
on-arrival: president = royalist_candidate_1932; chancellor = "Gallax"; chancellor_party = "Royalist"

[? if royalist_candidate_1932 == "Gallax" : Alaric Gallax of the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Royalists**</span> has won the presidency. He wastes no time in consolidating power. ?]
[? if royalist_candidate_1932 != "Gallax" : The <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Royalists**</span> candidate [+ president +] has won. The first action President [+ president +] takes is inviting Gallax back into the Commonwealth, and appointing him chancellor. The <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalists</span> waste no time in consolidating power. ?]

